WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.830
Big change on a small budget, finished safely and honestly.

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:11.320
This is the video for module three of Interior Decoration Basics: budgets, finishing and proof of results.

3
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:22.540
Most clients have modest budgets. A budget makeover is not a cheap-looking room. It is a room where every naira went to the change that made the biggest difference.

4
00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:27.070
You will learn to calculate paint, so nothing is wasted.

5
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.160
To finish the work to a safe, professional standard.

6
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:37.340
And to handle client money so openly that it becomes the reason they recommend you.

7
00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:47.250
First, declutter and clean. Remove what is broken, unused, or belongs in another room. This is free, and often the biggest change.

8
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:55.350
Second, rearrange existing furniture, using your floor plan to create a better layout and focal point.

9
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:01.970
Third, paint. Fresh walls, or one feature wall, transform a room for a modest cost.

10
00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:14.830
Then warm bulbs and a lamp, then soft furnishings like curtains and cushion covers. Adire, ankara offcuts, raffia baskets and clay pots give character at modest cost.

11
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:21.600
Replace furniture only if a piece is broken, unsafe, or completely the wrong size.

12
00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:36.630
Ifeoma's bedroom is 4.2 by 3.6 m, with a 2.7 m ceiling. Add the four walls for the perimeter: 15.6 m. Times the height, that is 42.1 square metres.

13
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:43.370
Take away the door and window, 3.7 square metres, to get 38.4.

14
00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.390
Two coats doubles it to 76.8.

15
00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:55.340
Her tin covers about 10 square metres per litre, so she needs about 8 litres, plus a little for touch-ups.

16
00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:09.790
If the client chooses just a feature wall behind the bed, it is about 2 litres. That costs far less and still changes the room. Get two prices for each big item, and add about 10% contingency.

17
00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:21.310
Tall furniture can tip over onto children. Fix wardrobes, bookcases and TV units to the wall with anti-tip straps or brackets, and secure TVs.

18
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:35.210
Before drilling, check for hidden cables and pipes. They often run straight up or down from switches and sockets. Wear eye protection, and hang heavy mirrors with proper fixings, not a single small nail.

19
00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:50.620
Secure rug edges and keep cables tidy, especially for older people. Keep fabrics away from cookers and candles, and never block exits. When sanding old furniture, wear a dust mask and keep windows open.

20
00:02:51.870 --> 00:03:04.050
Clients judge you by the details. Before you invite the client in, check that paint edges are clean with no drips, curtains hang level, art is straight, cables are hidden and the room is clean.

21
00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.650
Check it yourself. Do not leave it for the client to find.

22
00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:17.750
Kemi photographs every receipt immediately and records each purchase: date, item, seller and amount. These are illustrative figures.

23
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.460
She received 120,000 naira for materials.

24
00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:32.880
She spent 108,500. Her fabric seller gave a 3,000 naira discount, and she shows it on the receipt, as agreed.

25
00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:48.460
She sends the client the table, the receipt photos, and the balance of 11,500 naira. Never quietly add a hidden mark-up to receipts. The client can see every naira, and recommends Kemi to two friends.

26
00:03:49.710 --> 00:04:00.770
To remember. Declutter, rearrange and paint before you buy. Calculate litres from the net wall area, coats and coverage. Anchor tall furniture and check before drilling.

27
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:07.840
Share every receipt and discount. And take before and after photos from the same spots, without filters.

28
00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:25.450
Now practise. Plan a budget makeover with real prices and a 10% contingency. Run a quality and safety audit on a room. And document one project with before and after photos, a budget versus actual table, and the owner's feedback.

29
00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.740
Continue with the lessons below.
